  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1230 PM MDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nFrom Tuesday into Wednesday, another round of moist southwest flow \nwill develop over the region, and this will bring another round of \nshowers and storms to the region, with most of the heavier showers \nfalling south of US highway 50. The overall best chance of more \nwidespread heavier precip will occur wednesday afternoon with a \nheavier band of precip over the far eastern plains Wed evening. \n\nThursday and Friday will remain unsettled over the region with \nscattered showers and thunderstorms expected during the two day \nperiod. \n\nFor the weekend, it will be drier and warmer, with only isolated \nshowers and storms expected. Temps for the weekend will be in the \nmid 80s plains and 70s valleys.",
